    "summary": "The investigation identifies two primary causal branches: (1) A potential unrecorded service-routing change affecting instrument-air supply without proper ECP revision or temporary instruction attachment; and (2) The point register's inability to establish valve states, which limits detection of distribution disturbances. Both remain hypotheses due to missing evidence on whether a routing change occurred or if external factors caused the interruption.",
